MERGED glm-53-flash
Single arm, 230 lines, clippy 0.

Probed all ten behaviours. The one that carries it:

  good 5 >= min_trials 5, BUT bad 4 > max_bad 3  ->  Abandon(4), scorable=false

Enough measurements gathered alongside more failures than tolerated is NOT a
result. An instrument that flaked four times out of nine is suspect, and scoring
that run would blame a candidate for the harness.

The rest, all correct:
  bad == max_bad (3)          Run        tolerance means the limit is allowed
  bad == max_bad + 1          Abandon
  attempts exhausted, few     Abandon(0) never measured, not a failure
  attempts exhausted, enough  Enough(5)  the clause-5 pair, same attempts
  min_trials 0, good 0        Enough(0)  the manifest asked for no minimum
  max_attempts 0              Abandon    nothing may be attempted
  max_bad 0, one bad          Abandon(1)

scorable is true only for Enough, which is the point: Abandon is an ending that
yields a report about the instrument, not a score about the arm.
